WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.810
Welcome back, champ!

2
00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:19.560
Unit 2 · How Machines Learn · done!

3
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:29.680
Unit 3 · AI That Sees, Hears, and Talks

4
00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:34.380
Chapter 1 · Can Computers See?

5
00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:46.230
No eyeballs! So how can it see?

6
00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:58.890
Meet Kabir and his cat, Coco

7
00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:06.610
Kabir types "cat" in the photo app

8
00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:16.500
Whoosh! Every cat photo, found!

9
00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:24.410
How did the phone know? Think!

10
00:01:24.410 --> 00:01:34.840
But one Coco photo was missing…

11
00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:44.030
Let's zoom in on Coco's photo…

12
00:01:44.030 --> 00:01:57.280
Tiny coloured dots called PIXELS

13
00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:09.810
The computer sees dots, not a cat

14
00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:18.030
It looks for PATTERNS

15
00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:30.410
Clues: Edges · Shapes · Colours

16
00:02:30.410 --> 00:02:45.290
Every ball is round. That's a pattern!

17
00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:55.860
Pointy ears + whiskers → maybe a cat!

18
00:02:55.860 --> 00:03:07.660
It learns patterns from many examples

19
00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:22.180
Many bottle photos → tall shape + cap

20
00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:32.410
Computer vision = matching patterns in pixels

21
00:03:32.410 --> 00:03:39.620
Not magic. Not alive. Just patterns!

22
00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:51.540
Object spotting: what's on Kabir's table?

23
00:03:51.540 --> 00:04:08.920
Round → ball · Cap → bottle · Pages → book

24
00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:19.760
Face unlock matches your face's pattern

25
00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:26.880
Photo apps group dogs, beaches, and cats

26
00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:37.160
Some apps can name a flower from a photo

27
00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:43.820
Computers can be wrong!

28
00:04:43.820 --> 00:04:51.140
Dark light: the edges disappear

29
00:04:51.140 --> 00:05:01.800
Odd angle or tiny: a ball becomes a dot

30
00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:11.000
Partly hidden: only half the pattern

31
00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:24.720
Why did the app miss this Coco photo?

32
00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:35.250
Coco was hidden. Not enough pattern!

33
00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:57.670
Which photo is HARDEST to spot the cat in?

34
00:05:57.670 --> 00:06:09.370
Tiny + dark = hardest to spot!

35
00:06:09.370 --> 00:06:13.320
Your turn: practice check

36
00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:25.160
Why miss a black cat on a black sofa?

37
00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:37.740
Same colour → no edges → no cat shape

38
00:06:37.740 --> 00:06:44.410
Computers see pixels, not things

39
00:06:44.410 --> 00:06:49.170
Seeing = matching patterns

40
00:06:49.170 --> 00:06:52.690
Patterns are learned from many examples

41
00:06:52.690 --> 00:06:58.480
Dark, tiny, or hidden things can fool it

42
00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:04.390
Chapter 1 done!

43
00:07:04.390 --> 00:07:11.190
Next: Quiz · Tap Finish
